digraph ReasoningTree {
  rankdir="TB";
  "I1" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Currently collective migration is a hallmark, and commonly adhesion strength determines mode, so adhesion regulates collective migration."];
  "I10" [label="(0,0,0) abduction-reasoning: Phenomenon: Contribution unclear, and Knowledge: Lack of tools is challenge, so a new tool is needed."];
  "I14" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Case: Connections lead to collective movement, and Common: Adhesions made cells faster, so adhesions promote collective speed."];
  "I2" [label="(0,0,0) deduction-reasoning: Currently cadherins link cells and catenins to cytoskeleton, and if they connect and signal then they regulate dynamics, so cadherins are key transducers."];
  "I4" [label="(0,0,0) abduction-reasoning: Phenomenon: Membrane signaling overlooked, and Knowledge: Membrane regarded as passive, so the passive view is questioned."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Investigate whether artificially reinforcing cell-cell contacts solely at the plasma membrane with photoswitchable Cph1 adhesions, without direct linkage to the actin cytoskeleton, elevates membrane tension, engages PLD2-PA-mTOR signaling, and shifts individually migrating cells into faster coordinated collective cell migration, thereby testing a cytoskeleton-independent membrane-derived mechanism for controlling collective migration.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) A membrane-focused adhesion perturbation can be interpreted cautiously by separating what the tool directly changes, what phenotypes are observed, and what mechanistic pathway is being tested, without claiming that membrane tension alone has been isolated as the sole sufficient cause."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Given that plasma membrane-derived signals in collective migration remain unclear because tools are lacking, artificial photoswitchable Cph1 adhesions are a plausible tool for probing cell-cell adhesions without direct linkage to the actin cytoskeleton."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) In the photoactivated adhesion setting, increased cell-cell adhesions are reported to increase membrane tension, and PLD2 activation is framed as leading to PA production and mTOR signaling activation."];
  "S1" [label="(1,0,0) Currently collective cell migration is a hallmark of morphogenesis, tissue homeostasis, and wound healing."];
  "S12" [label="(12,0,0) Phenomenon: The contribution of plasma membrane-derived signals to collective cell migration remains unclear when independent of adhesion-cytoskeleton links."];
  "S13" [label="(13,0,0) Knowledge: A significant challenge is the lack of tools capable of dissecting mechanical cues at the plasma membrane from mechano-transduction through adhesion molecules."];
  "S16" [label="(16,0,0) If artificial photoswitchable cell-cell adhesions based on Cph1 are used, then they induce adhesions without directly linking to the actin cytoskeleton."];
  "S17" [label="(17,0,0) Case: An increase in cell-cell connections leads to coordinated and collective cell movement in cells that otherwise would migrate as single cells."];
  "S18" [label="(18,0,0) Common: Increased cell-cell adhesions made cells faster rather than slowing them down as expected from friction."];
  "S19" [label="(19,0,0) Currently the photoactivated increase in cell-cell adhesions resulted in an increase in membrane tension at the cellular level."];
  "S2" [label="(2,0,0) Commonly, the strength of intercellular adhesions determines whether cells migrate collectively or individually."];
  "S20" [label="(20,0,0) If the photoactivated increase in cell-cell adhesions activated PLD2, then it resulted in increased PA and activation of mTOR signaling."];
  "S3" [label="(3,0,0) Currently cell-cell adhesions mediated by classical cadherins link neighboring cells and recruit catenins to the cytoskeleton."];
  "S4" [label="(4,0,0) If cadherins mechanically connect cells and activate signaling circuits, then they regulate cytoskeletal dynamics and gene expression."];
  "S5" [label="(5,0,0) Phenomenon: The contribution of signaling cues originating directly from the plasma membrane in collective cell dynamics has been largely overlooked."];
  "S6" [label="(6,0,0) Knowledge: The membrane is often regarded as a passive structure enabling signal transduction via transmembrane protein complexes."];
  "S1" -> "I1" [label="induction-case"];
  "S2" -> "I1" [label="induction-common"];
  "S3" -> "I2" [label="deduction-case"];
